```
(License header/Javadoc omitted for brevity; verbatim signatures above.) Implementations exist under `repository/springdatajpa/`, `repository/jpa/`, and `repository/jdbc/`.

---

## 6. Escalation handlers relevant to creating owners

Escalation YAMLs live in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/`. Each maps an exception type to a handler class. Owner-create-relevant ones:

**`...MissingOwnerFieldsException.yml`**
```yaml
handle:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler
```
**`...DuplicateTelephoneException.yml`**
```yaml
handle:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler
```
Also present and relevant to the create flow: `...InvalidEmailException.yml`, `...InvalidTelephoneException.yml`, plus generic ones (`java.lang.Exception.yml`, `MethodArgumentNotValidException.yml`, `DataIntegrityViolationException.yml`, `AuthorizationDeniedException.yml`, `NotFoundException.yml`).

Exception + handler classes (all in `.../rest/escalation/`):

- **`MissingOwnerFieldsException.java`** — `extends Exception`, carries `List<String> fields` (offending field names).
- **`MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler.java`** — returns HTTP **400** with a `ProblemDetail`, setting an `errors` array = the missing field names.
- **`DuplicateTelephoneException.java`** — `extends Exception`, message includes the telephone.
- **`DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler.java`** — returns HTTP **409 Conflict** `ProblemDetail`.
- **`InvalidEmailException.java`** / **`InvalidEmailExceptionHandler.java`** — invalid email.
- **`InvalidTelephoneException.java`** / **`InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler.java`** — telephone that cannot normalize; **400**.
- **`ProblemDetails.java`** (package-private helper) — builds the common `ProblemDetail` body (title = exception simple name, `about:blank` type, `timestamp`, empty `schemaValidationErrors`). Full contents shown below since the exact shape is load-bearing:

```java
final class ProblemDetails {
    private ProblemDetails() {}
    static ProblemDetail build(Exception ex, HttpStatus status, String detail) {
        ProblemDetail problemDetail = ProblemDetail.forStatus(status);
        problemDetail.setType(URI.create("about:blank"));
        problemDetail.setTitle(ex.getClass().getSimpleName());
        problemDetail.setDetail(detail);
        problemDetail.setProperty("timestamp", Instant.now());
        problemDetail.setProperty("schemaValidationErrors", List.<ValidationMessageDto>of());
        return problemDetail;
    }
}
```

---

## 7. Tests for creating owners

Tests live under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`. They are black-box acceptance tests driving `POST /api/owners`.

**`AcceptanceTest.java`** — three tests around a "household-duplicate" rule:
- `coreRejectsSameLastNameAndAddress` — creating a second owner with the same `lastName` + `address` expects **409 Conflict**.
- `functionalityAllowsDifferentAddress` — same lastName, different address expects 2xx.
- `functionalityAllowsWithSharesHousehold` — same lastName + address but `sharesHousehold=true` expects 2xx.

Note: these assert behavior (409 for same lastName+address, `sharesHousehold` override) that is **not** implemented in the current POST pipeline shown above — the pipeline only dedups on telephone, not on lastName+address, and nothing reads `sharesHousehold`. So these acceptance tests describe intended/target behavior that the current functions do not yet satisfy.

**`AcceptanceBase.java`** — the harness (`@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(roles OWNER_ADMIN/VET_ADMIN/ADMIN)`). Key helpers:
- `createOwner(body)` -> `POST /api/owners`, `createOwnerOk(body)` asserts 2xx and returns the new id (from body `id` or `Location` header).
- `ownerNode()` builds a fully-valid unique owner (firstName `Test`, unique lastName `Sur…`, unique address, city, `04XXXXXXXX` telephone).
- `getOwner(id)`, `fetchOwner(id)`, `deleteOwner(id)`, `createOwnerWithKey(body, key)` (Idempotency-Key), `fillCity`, `createMany`.
- Pinned reference data (city->region, region->timezone, postcode ranges, 2026 holidays) and helpers (`sha256hex`, `shaHex`, `luhn`, `toBusinessDay`).

**`AuditLogCapture.java`** — an audit-log test support component (also owner-related).

---

## 8. Build & test

- Build tool: **Maven**, with a wrapper. `pom.xml` at `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml`; artifact `spring-petclinic-rest`; parent `spring-boot-starter-parent`. Wrapper present at `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw`.
- Run tests: `./mvnw test` (or `./mvnw verify`). Full build: `./mvnw clean install`. Tests use JUnit 5 + Spring Boot test + `woof_test` (OfficeFloor test support) + MockMvc.
- Code generation: `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` (7.23.0) generates the DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto`, `OwnerPageDto`, `ValidationMessageDto`, etc.) from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java` (package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`) — so a build is required before those DTO types resolve. MapStruct (`mapstruct` + `mapstruct-processor`) generates the `OwnerMapper` implementation.

### Key takeaway
The current `POST /api/owners` pipeline validates required fields, normalizes telephone (E.164) and email, assigns `registrationDate` and a `customerCode`, rejects duplicate telephones (409), saves, and returns 201 Created with `OwnerDto`. The acceptance tests in `src/test` additionally expect lastName+address household-duplicate rejection and a `sharesHousehold` override, which the shown pipeline does not yet implement.

